          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. Folded Footprint and Ceiling Height</h2>
<p>
            A folding treadmill is sold on its folded size, but you live with three measurements, not
            one: the floor it covers when folded, the height it stands to when folded, and the room it
            needs while you are using it. Here are the makers' figures side by side, converted to
            square feet so they are easier to compare with the corner you have in mind.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[640px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Machine</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">In use (L x W)</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Folded floor area</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Folded height</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Unit weight</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Horizon T101 Connect</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">70.5 x 33.5 in. (16.4 sq ft)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10.9 sq ft</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">61 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">180 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Horizon 7.0 AT</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">76 x 35 in. (18.5 sq ft)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10.7 sq ft</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">68 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">277 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">NordicTrack T Series 10</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">75.1 x 34.3 in. (17.9 sq ft)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About 9.7 sq ft (retailer figure)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About 68 in. (retailer figure)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not confirmed; 250 lb boxed</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">ProForm Carbon TLS</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">67.5 x 31.6 in. (14.8 sq ft)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7.2 sq ft (ProForm only)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">65.7 in. (ProForm only)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not published; 205 lb boxed</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sole F65</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">77 x 36 in. (19.3 sq ft)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">12.0 sq ft (Sole only)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">66 in. (Sole only)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not on Sole's page</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">UREVO Strol 2E</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">51.2 x 22.6 in. (8.0 sq ft)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lies flat; slides under furniture</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4.6 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">47.2 lb</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Two things stand out. First, folding saves less floor than people expect: a folded
            treadmill still covers 7 to 12 square feet, roughly the size of an armchair, and you need
            somewhere to put it that is not a walkway. Second, the machine with the most generous
            deck is not always the biggest folded. The 7.0 AT, with a 60-inch running deck, folds to a
            slightly smaller floor area than the T101 Connect, because it stands taller instead. The
            Sole F65 is the largest folded machine here on its maker's figures.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Folded height against the room, not just the ceiling</h3>
          <p>
            Folded heights here run from 61 to 68 inches, so a standard 8-foot ceiling is never the
            problem when the machine is stored. What catches people out is everything else at that
            height: a window sill, a wall cupboard, a sloped attic ceiling, a radiator shelf, or the
            underside of a staircase. Measure the exact spot where it will stand, to the lowest
            obstruction above it, and leave a few inches for the deck to swing through as it rises.
            A deck sweeps through an arc as it folds, and that arc can be deeper than the folded
            footprint suggests.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Ceiling height while you use it</h3>
          <p>
            In use, the ceiling matters much more. A working rule is your height, plus the step-up
            height of the deck, plus several inches for the bounce of each stride — more if you run,
            and more again at steep incline, which lifts the front of the deck. Step-up heights here
            run from about 7 inches on the T101 Connect to about 8.6 inches on the 7.0 AT. For a
            6-foot runner that comes to roughly 86 to 90 inches, which fits under an 8-foot ceiling
            but not comfortably under a low basement beam. Our guide to
            <a href="/treadmill-dimensions-space-requirements/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill dimensions and space requirements</a>
            sets out the clearances behind and beside the deck as well, and the manual for your unit
            takes precedence over any rule of thumb.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="fold-weight-wheels" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">4. Soft-Drop Folding, Weight and Wheels</h2>
<p>
            In a small home a folding treadmill only saves space if it actually gets folded, and that
            depends on how the fold works, how heavy the machine is, and whether you can move it once
            it is up. Those three are worth checking before you pay, because no discount makes a fold
            you dread any easier.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>How the deck comes down.</strong> Horizon describes both of its machines here as
            having "one-step hydraulic folding": you lift the deck until it locks, and a gas strut
            lowers it under control when you release it. NordicTrack describes the T Series 10 as
            folding with assisted lowering, and ProForm calls the <a href="/proform-carbon-tls-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Carbon TLS</a> fold EasyLift. Sole's
            current F65 page describes a "Kick Release" fold and does not say in so many words
            whether the descent is damped, so ask the seller before you assume it. A controlled
            descent is not a luxury in a flat: a deck that drops freely is loud, can damage the floor
            and is a real hazard to feet, children and pets. If a listing does not say how the deck
            is lowered, assume it is not assisted until the seller tells you otherwise. Our guide on
            <a href="/how-to-fold-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how to fold a treadmill</a>
            covers the lock checks to do every time.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>How heavy it is to move.</strong> Folding is one job; moving the folded machine is
            another. Horizon lists the T101 Connect at 180 lb and the 7.0 AT at 277 lb. ProForm and
            NordicTrack publish boxed weights (205 lb and 250 lb) rather than machine weights, and
            Sole's current F65 page gives no weight at all. Those numbers decide whether one person
            can tip the folded machine onto its wheels and roll it across a room, or whether it will,
            in practice, stay where it was assembled. If you plan to roll it out of a cupboard and back
            every day, the lighter machines here are the realistic ones. If you will park it once and
            leave it, weight matters far less than deck length.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Wheels and floors.</strong> Most folding treadmills have small transport wheels at
            the front, which work on hard floors and much less well on thick carpet or across a
            threshold strip. Check where the wheels sit, whether the machine has to be tipped to
            engage them, and whether your route from storage spot to use spot has a step or a rug in
            it. For moves between rooms or flats, our guide to
            <a href="/how-to-move-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">moving a treadmill</a>
            explains how to do it without damaging the frame or the floor.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>The compact option is different.</strong> The UREVO Strol 2E does not fold upright
            at all. It folds its handlebar flat and the whole 47 lb pad slides under a bed or sofa,
            which is why it suits a studio where nothing can stand against a wall. That convenience
            comes with a short, narrow belt and a walking-pad motor, as its card explains.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="discounts" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">5. What Folding Treadmill Discounts Usually Look Like</h2>
<p>
            Folding treadmills from the big home-fitness brands are on promotion for most of the year,
            which makes Black Friday harder to read, not easier. The pattern on the machines here is
            consistent, and once you see it the headline percentages stop mattering.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>The reference price is often a number nobody pays.</strong> Horizon showed the 7.0
            AT at $1,099 against a $2,100 "regular" price on 28 October, and the T101 Connect at $699
            against $999. A banner calling the 7.0 AT "half price" on Black Friday would be measuring
            against that $2,100, which Horizon does not charge. The useful benchmark is the best price
            the machine has actually sold for recently — for the 7.0 AT, $934 with a Horizon code on
            14 October.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Codes and retailers move more than list prices.</strong> On the same days we saw
            the Carbon TLS at $1,099.99 on ProForm's store and $799.99 at <a href="/scheels-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Scheels</a>, and the T Series 10
            at $1,599.99 on NordicTrack's store and $1,299 at P.C. Richard. A $300 spread between two
            authorised sellers on the same day is larger than many Black Friday discounts. That is
            why our targets are set against the lowest price we could source, not the maker's own
            store.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Genuine reductions are usually modest.</strong> Our
            <a href="/treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Black Friday method guide</a>
            puts a genuine treadmill discount in a strong sale window at roughly 15 to 30% off the
            normal selling price. On a folding treadmill that already sells well below its reference
            price, a further $100 to $200 is a realistic good deal; $50 is not worth waiting for if you
            need the machine now. Sole's own range showed $100 to $200 off every in-stock model on
            13 October, which gives a sense of how discounts there tend to look.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Price it delivered.</strong> A folding treadmill box is still 200 to 330 lb for
            the full machines here, and delivery tiers vary: kerbside, inside the door, room of choice
            and assembly. If you live up two flights of stairs, a cheaper price with kerbside delivery
            can cost more in the end than a dearer one carried in and built. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-delivery-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill delivery guide</a>
            explains the tiers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="model-number" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">6. Check the Exact Model Number Before You Buy</h2>
<p>
            Black Friday is when old stock, previous generations and near-identical sibling models
            are cleared at prices that look like deals on the current machine. Folding treadmills are
            especially prone to this because the names stay the same for years while the machines
            change. Before you pay, match the model number or SKU on the listing against the maker's
            own current product page. On the machines here, these are the traps we found.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Horizon T101.</strong> Amazon search shows the current T101 Connect alongside an older T101 marked as the "old model", a T101-3 and a T101-04. The current model is the T101 Connect, SKU HTM1483-01. Older T101-05 units were recalled in October 2022 over unexpected speed changes; that recall does not cover the Connect, but it is a reason to check the model on any unusually cheap listing.</li>
            <li><strong>Horizon 7.0 AT.</strong> The current version is SKU HTM1457-01. Older 7.0 AT figures — 253 lb, different dimensions — still turn up in search results and describe an earlier machine. Apple Watch and GymKit pairing is a quick check that you are looking at the current one.</li>
            <li><strong>NordicTrack T Series.</strong> The current T Series 10 is model NTL15425. The T Series 5 and T Series 8 are cheaper retail-only machines under the same series name, and older T 6.5 S and similar names still circulate. The T Series 5 is the one whose fold we could not confirm.</li>
            <li><strong>ProForm Carbon TLS.</strong> The model number is PFTL79925. Carbon T7, Carbon T10 and Carbon TL are different, older machines.</li>
            <li><strong>Sole F65.</strong> Sole's 2026 F65 lists a 20 by 60-inch deck and a 350 lb user limit. Earlier F65s were described with a 22-inch deck and a 325 lb limit. A discounted F65 may be either, so get the model year in writing.</li>
            <li><strong>UREVO Strol 2E.</strong> At least one Amazon listing titled "Strol 2E" describes a 12% incline and a 300 lb limit, which belong to the Strol 2E Pro. The Strol 2E is flat and lists 265 lb.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Also read the seller line near the buy button. A listing sold by Amazon or by the brand's
            own store carries the manufacturer's warranty without question; a third-party reseller
            at a suspiciously low price may be selling older stock, a return, or a machine the brand
            will not cover.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="timeline" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">7. When the 2026 Deals Start</h2>
<p>
            Black Friday 2026 is Friday 27 November, after Thanksgiving on Thursday 26 November, and
            <a href="/cyber-monday-treadmill-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Cyber Monday</a> is 30 November. Amazon had not announced its 2026 Black Friday dates when we
            wrote this on 28 October. In recent years its Black Friday week has typically started
            about a week before Thanksgiving and run through Cyber Monday, and the makers' own stores
            usually start their promotions around the same time or earlier.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Now to early November.</strong> Choose your shortlist and measure the space. Note today's prices so you have a benchmark: the figures on this page are a start. Horizon's current free-shipping offer on its Studio treadmills, which include the 7.0 AT, was marked as ending on 1 November.</li>
            <li><strong>The week before Thanksgiving.</strong> Typically when Amazon's Black Friday week opens and the first real reductions appear. Check stock as well as price; the T101 Connect was sold out at Horizon on 28 October, and the 7.0 AT was showing a ship date in the week of 2 November.</li>
            <li><strong>Black Friday to Cyber Monday.</strong> Prices can change between these days, in either direction. If a machine on your list hits your target, buying it is usually wiser than gambling on a further drop that may not come.</li>
            <li><strong>After you buy.</strong> If the price falls within your return window, ask the seller about a price adjustment and get the answer in writing. Policies differ, and we did not find a published one for every seller here.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Delivery lead time matters more for folding treadmills than for most purchases, because
            these are freight items. If you want the machine before the holidays, check the delivery
            estimate at checkout, not just the price.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="folding-or-not" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">8. Do You Need a Folding Treadmill at All?</h2>
<p>
            It is worth asking before the sale starts, because the answer changes which deals matter.
            Folding costs something: at the same price, a <a href="/best-non-folding-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>non-folding treadmill</a> tends to have a
            heavier, steadier frame, and some of the best running decks do not fold at all. Our
            comparison of
            <a href="/folding-vs-non-folding-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">folding and non-folding treadmills</a>
            sets out that trade properly.
          </p>
          <p>
            A folding treadmill is the right choice if the machine genuinely has to give floor back —
            a living room that is also the gym, a spare room that is sometimes a guest room, a flat
            where a 19-square-foot machine left open would be the dominant piece of furniture. It is
            the wrong choice if the treadmill will stay unfolded in practice, which is common with
            heavy machines and with any fold that takes real effort. Be honest about which you are.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you decide on folding, the next question is whether you need a treadmill or a pad.
            A walking pad like the Strol 2E stores flat and costs a fraction of the price, but it is a
            walking machine with a short belt. If you will jog regularly, or if more than one person
            will use it, a full folding treadmill with at least a 55-inch deck is the safer buy, and a
            60-inch deck if anyone runs. Our evergreen
            <a href="/best-folding-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best folding treadmills</a>
            guide covers the category beyond this sale, and our
            <a href="/black-friday-treadmill-deals-under-1000/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Black Friday deals under $1,000</a>
            page includes non-folding options if you have room after all.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">9. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Will folding treadmills be cheaper on Black Friday 2026?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Probably, but nobody can promise a price. Black Friday 2026 prices had not been published when we wrote this on 28 October. Late November is usually one of the strongest treadmill sale windows, and on folding machines that already sell well below their reference prices, a further $100 to $200 is a realistic good deal. Judge any offer against the lowest recent selling price, not the "regular" price.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">When do Amazon’s Black Friday folding treadmill deals start?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Amazon had not announced its 2026 dates when we wrote this. Its Black Friday week has typically started about a week before Thanksgiving, which falls on 26 November in 2026, and run through Cyber Monday on 30 November. Makers’ own stores often start promotions around the same time.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best folding treadmill for a small apartment?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Of the machines here, the Horizon T101 Connect suits most people: a 55-inch deck, one-step hydraulic folding, 180 lb and a 61-inch folded height. If floor space is the hardest limit, the ProForm Carbon TLS has the smallest folded footprint on ProForm’s figures. If nothing can stand against a wall, a flat-folding pad like the UREVO Strol 2E slides under a bed.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much space does a folded treadmill take?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The full machines here cover about 7 to 12 square feet folded and stand 61 to 68 inches tall, on the makers’ figures. Measure the exact storage spot to the lowest obstruction above it, and leave room for the deck to swing up. In use they need 15 to 19 square feet plus clearance behind and beside the deck.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is a soft-drop or hydraulic fold, and does it matter?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It is a gas strut that lowers the deck slowly when you unfold the machine, instead of letting it fall. In a small home it matters: a free-falling deck is loud, can damage floors and is a hazard to feet, children and pets. Horizon lists one-step hydraulic folding on both of its machines here; check the listing or ask the seller for any other model.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a walking pad a good alternative to a folding treadmill?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For walking, often yes: pads like the UREVO Strol 2E fold flat to under 5 inches and cost a fraction of the price. For regular jogging or running, no. Their belts are short and narrow and their motors are built for walking. If anyone in the home will run, a folding treadmill with a 60-inch deck is the safer buy.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Folding Treadmill on Black Friday</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Each of these turns a good price into a poor purchase, and each is specific to buying a folding machine for a small home.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Measuring the floor but not the height</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Folded treadmills here stand 61 to 68 inches tall, and the deck sweeps through an arc as it rises. A window sill, wall cupboard, sloped ceiling or stair underside can block a spot that has plenty of floor. Measure to the lowest obstruction above the storage spot before you buy.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every fold is soft-drop</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Some folding treadmills lower the deck under control with a gas strut; others rely on you to lower it by hand. A free-falling deck is loud and dangerous in a small home. If the listing does not describe how the deck is lowered, ask the seller before you order.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a machine too heavy to move</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A 277 lb treadmill folds, but it will not be rolled out of a cupboard every evening. If you need to move it daily, choose by machine weight and wheel placement as well as folded size, and check the route for rugs, steps and threshold strips.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not checking the model number on the deal</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Black Friday clears old stock and previous generations under current names. The Horizon T101, Sole F65 and UREVO Strol 2E all have older or sibling versions with different figures. Match the model number or SKU on the listing to the maker’s current product page before you pay.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

